# state: first-run   (recorded on a disk with no save for the title (NOTES.md E); lane.savestate433)
# Buffy the Vampire Slayer (45410012), Nova. Built from the generic survey
# 1790928774-titleroutes-2773088 (lane.titleroutes session 65, 2026-10-02),
# which reached live play. Read from its route-frames (copied to
# scratch/judge/), not guessed:
#   booted (012801): the intro FMV (Buffy in fog).
#   cycle 1 (012807 START / 012813 A): START skips to the Buffy title; A
#     opens the main menu (Start Game / Load Game / Options / Extras).
#   cycle 2 (012819 START / 012825 A): START picks Start Game ("Launch a New
#     Game on your Xbox Hard Disk called Buffy 1"); A confirms -> DIFFICULTY
#     (Normal lit).
#   cycle 3 (012830 START / 012836 A): START confirms Normal -> "Summoning"
#     (loading), then the mission card "Spanish Mission, Outskirts of
#     Sunnydale, Sunday 11:53PM" (FPS 7 while it loads).
#   cycle 4 (012843 START / 012849 A): live play in the canyon, HUD at top
#     left, "TIP: Move the R thumbstick..." banner.
#   cycles 5-14: START pauses (PAUSE: Resume / Options / Quit, Resume lit)
#     and A resumes, so every later cycle toggles pause and back.
# A START/A pair in play is therefore a no-op (pause, Resume), which makes
# one extra cycle a cheap guard against a slower load. Then a play loop with
# NO START: walk forward with the left stick, turn now and then, attack. The
# survey's loop swung the camera stick (RX) and its play frames show mostly
# sky; this one leaves the camera alone.
# Disk state: Start Game writes a new save ("Buffy 1"). A second run on a
# disk that already holds one may name it Buffy 2 or ask to overwrite; this
# route has only been read from a run on a disk with no Buffy save.
# DRAFT until a dispatch run replays it and its frames from the mark on are
# reviewed.
wait 20
shot boot20
wait 20
shot boot40
wait 20
shot booted
repeat 5 {
    press START
    wait 5
    shot menu-start
    press A
    wait 5
    shot menu-a
}
wait 3
shot pre-mark
mark gameplay               # CHECK: the canyon with the HUD, no PAUSE panel
# Replay 1790931264-titleroutes-3615749 (session 65) moved for ~1 min, then
# sat 4 min on one frame (sky and a tree) under the tip "Run and press B to
# jump between ledges": the canyon has gaps that need a running jump, and the
# first loop never pressed B. So: run forward and jump (B) twice per cycle,
# and turn for longer (1.5 s) so a wall does not hold her for the window.
repeat forever {
    axis LY min
    wait 2
    press B
    wait 1.5
    press B
    wait 2
    press A
    wait 0.6
    press X
    wait 1
    axis LX max
    wait 1.5
    axis LX mid
    wait 2
    press B
    wait 2
    press A
    wait 0.6
    press A
    wait 1
    axis LX min
    wait 1.5
    axis LX mid
    wait 1
    shot play
}
